From 69f3d1c82cddae0de8187d73be07cbde0d27a36c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tom de Vries <tdevries@suse.de>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 15:05:48 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] [gdb/testsuite] Fix FAIL in gdb.tui/tui-mode-switch.exp

With test-case gdb.tui/tui-mode-switch.exp I ran into:
...
PASS: $exp: enter TUI
^[[?1006;1000l^[[12;1H^[[?1049l^[[23;0;0t^M^[[?1l^[>PASS: $exp: exit TUI
Box Dump (40 x 1) @ (0, 11):
   11
Box Dump (40 x 1) @ (0, 11):
   11
Box Dump (40 x 1) @ (0, 11):
   11
Box Dump (40 x 1) @ (0, 11):
   11
Box Dump (40 x 1) @ (0, 11):
   11
Box Dump (40 x 1) @ (0, 11):
   11
b(gdb) bBox Dump (40 x 1) @ (0, 11):
   11 b(gdb) b
WARNING: timeout in accept_gdb_output
Screen Dump (size 40 columns x 12 rows, cursor at column 8, row 11):
    0 (gdb)
    1 (gdb)
    2 (gdb)
    3 (gdb)
    4 (gdb)
    5 (gdb)
    6 (gdb)
    7 (gdb)
    8 (gdb)
    9 (gdb)
   10 (gdb)
   11 b(gdb) b
FAIL: $exp: type b
...

The FAIL happens in this part of the test:
...
 # Enter TUI.
 send_gdb "\030\001"
 gdb_assert { [Term::wait_for ""] } "enter TUI"

 # Exit TUI.
 send_gdb "\030\001"
 gdb_assert { [Term::wait_for ""] } "exit TUI"

 # Type b.
 send_gdb "b"
...

It's a bit easier to see what happens if we switch on logging in Term::_log
using verbose -log:
...
PASS: $exp: enter TUI
^[[?1006;1000l^[[12;1H^[[?1049l^[[23;0;0t^M^[[?1l^[>+++ wait_for: ESC
+++ wait_for: CSI
+++ wait_for: _csi_0x3f_l <<<?>>>
+++ ignored: Disable SGR Mouse Mode
+++ ignored: Don't send Mouse X & Y on button press and release
PASS: $exp: exit TUI
...

The wait_for for "exit TUI" triggers on the prompt of the TUI that's still
there, so "b" is typed too early.

From there on, there's a short window between endwin in tui_disable and
emitting the prompt where echo is enabled.  If the b arrives in that window,
we get "b(gdb) b".

We can reproduce the FAIL reliably by adding a 200ms sleep after endwin in
tui_disable.

Fix this by waiting on the CLI prompt on the line where we're expecting it.

I checked that reverting commit ee3c07a28be ("[gdb/tui] Clear readline buffer
on switching to TUI") still makes the test-case fail.

Tested on x86_64-linux, both with and without the reproducer delay.

Bug: https://sourceware.org/bugzilla/show_bug.cgi?id=34737
---
 gdb/testsuite/gdb.tui/tui-mode-switch.exp | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/gdb/testsuite/gdb.tui/tui-mode-switch.exp b/gdb/testsuite/gdb.tui/tui-mode-switch.exp
index c60596213b8..e9318dadf8b 100644
--- a/gdb/testsuite/gdb.tui/tui-mode-switch.exp
+++ b/gdb/testsuite/gdb.tui/tui-mode-switch.exp
@@ -39,7 +39,8 @@ gdb_assert { [Term::wait_for ""] } "enter TUI"
 
 # Exit TUI.
 send_gdb "\030\001"
-gdb_assert { [Term::wait_for ""] } "exit TUI"
+gdb_assert { [Term::wait_for_region_contents {*}$line "^$gdb_prompt "] } \
+    "exit TUI"
 
 # Type b.
 send_gdb "b"

